(2804353, 387778, 62187, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised by the results. I thought your photo would do much better...it''s just not a topic one sees everyday. Now that I look again, I can see some dust and it could have been just a touch darker on the persons body...but still...these voters can be loco! Keep up the good work...</td>', 'I''m surprised by the results. I thought your photo would do much better...it''s just not a topic one sees everyday. Now that I look again, I can see some dust and it could have been just a touch darker on the persons body...but still...these voters can be loco! Keep up the good work...', '2006-09-06 09:36:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2804359, 384206, 62634, '<td valign="top">==========================<br/> <br/>Wow thats whats great about this form you really find out what you need to work on.  Obviously my horizon is tilted not just in this shot but another I submitted.  The shot is underexposed a bit I liked the mood it created, but may have affected the quality.  The comments were great and I appreciate them all.<br/></td>', '========================== Wow thats whats great about this form you really find out what you need to work on.  Obviously my horizon is tilted not just in this shot but another I submitted.  The shot is underexposed a bit I liked the mood it created, but may have affected the quality.  The comments were great and I appreciate them all.', '2006-09-06 09:37:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2804398, 387331, 59847, '<td valign="top">Hey all,<br/>Thanks for the votes, comments and critique, I do appreciate it very much. My interpretation of the silhouette was stretched a little here and a few of you guys liked it, and some obviously didn''t. But that''s OK, this is a democracy/popularity vote. From the comments it sounds as if this photo might have been better for another challenge topic. I am still very happy, I got my first fav and 10! :), and, I''m still learning and having fun. What''s better than that? <br/>Christian<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-09-06 08:53:00.</i></td>', 'Hey all,Thanks for the votes, comments and critique, I do appreciate it very much. My interpretation of the silhouette was stretched a little here and a few of you guys liked it, and some obviously didn''t. But that''s OK, this is a democracy/popularity vote. From the comments it sounds as if this photo might have been better for another challenge topic. I am still very happy, I got my first fav and 10! :), and, I''m still learning and having fun. What''s better than that? Christian', '2006-09-06 09:44:26.000000', '2006-09-06 09:53:00.000000', 0),
