(2805939, 384708, 62095, '<td valign="top">Since you asked... <br/> <br/>I''m fairly sure that Captain Jack was lost with the Pearl when it was attacked by the Kraken in POTC2.  However, chances are that it''ll be found again as POTC3 is about the characters searching for Captain Jack "beyond the grave", so he''d be with the ship.</td>', 'Since you asked...  I''m fairly sure that Captain Jack was lost with the Pearl when it was attacked by the Kraken in POTC2.  However, chances are that it''ll be found again as POTC3 is about the characters searching for Captain Jack "beyond the grave", so he''d be with the ship.', '2006-09-06 15:15:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2806239, 387140, 53316, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hokie:</b></div><hr/><i> To explain my vote of a 4.  </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks! This was indeed helpful.<br/> <br/>I tried smoothing out the background and it probably would have been more well-received, but I just didn''t prefer it. I liked the "old science textbook" feel of the grain.  But I definitely knew from the outset this wasn''t going to grab the attention of many (maybe the attention of those who hate spiders, hehe) and I am incredibly pleased this scored over a 5.<br/> <br/>Thank you <b>all</b> for your comments!</td>', 'Originally posted by hokie: To explain my vote of a 4.    Thanks! This was indeed helpful. I tried smoothing out the background and it probably would have been more well-received, but I just didn''t prefer it. I liked the "old science textbook" feel of the grain.  But I definitely knew from the outset this wasn''t going to grab the attention of many (maybe the attention of those who hate spiders, hehe) and I am incredibly pleased this scored over a 5. Thank you all for your comments!', '2006-09-06 16:25:25.000000', NULL, 0),
