(2818314, 384765, 55838, '<td valign="top">Back from vacation to see that you finished very well.  I''m glad - I loved this one.  Congratulations!  I was off slightly with my earlier prediction as 15th was straight B&amp;W &amp; finshed slightly ahead of you.  Still....maybe I have some special powers?  Hee hee!  :)  Great job on top 20 in a challenge full of stiff competition.</td>', 'Back from vacation to see that you finished very well.  I''m glad - I loved this one.  Congratulations!  I was off slightly with my earlier prediction as 15th was straight B&W & finshed slightly ahead of you.  Still....maybe I have some special powers?  Hee hee!  :)  Great job on top 20 in a challenge full of stiff competition.', '2006-09-09 19:05:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2818521, 386920, 55838, '<td valign="top">Whoooooaaa...a 4.9??  I am confused why this shot did not get 5+.  Nice colors and interesting silhouettes.  And I did notice the tiny spider even before reading your comments...not sure why it popped out at me (probably because of my phobia!)  Well - from one of your 51 "6" voters, I offer a hearty "huh?"</td>', 'Whoooooaaa...a 4.9??  I am confused why this shot did not get 5+.  Nice colors and interesting silhouettes.  And I did notice the tiny spider even before reading your comments...not sure why it popped out at me (probably because of my phobia!)  Well - from one of your 51 "6" voters, I offer a hearty "huh?"', '2006-09-09 20:20:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2818550, 386138, 52449, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mpreslar:</b></div><hr/><i> Well done! What Corp is it, BTW?</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I believe it was the Long Beach Concert Band. Just the drummers (snare, tenor, and bass) were having a reunion. There were drummers in their 20''s up to the 50''s+ in age. They assembled on the walkway at the beach early one evening to have a impromptu jam session. <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by mpreslar: Well done! What Corp is it, BTW?  I believe it was the Long Beach Concert Band. Just the drummers (snare, tenor, and bass) were having a reunion. There were drummers in their 20''s up to the 50''s+ in age. They assembled on the walkway at the beach early one evening to have a impromptu jam session. ', '2006-09-09 20:35:06.000000', NULL, 0),
